IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa21-part29-fraudulent-trading.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 29 -- Fraudulent trading (s 993).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Reading a result: see the header of coa21-ch1-panel.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING).

§ `Part 29: Fraudulent trading`

-- s 993(1): if any business of a company is carried on with intent to defraud creditors, or for any fraudulent purpose, every person knowingly a party to it commits an offence.
-- src:13927 | (1) If any business of a company is carried on with intent to defraud creditors of the company or creditors of any other person, or for any fraudulent purpose, every person who is knowingly a party to the carrying on of the business in that manner commits an offence.
@ref s 993(1) Offence of fraudulent trading (src:13927-13927)
GIVEN `any business of a company is carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carried on with intent to defraud creditors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carried on with intent to defraud creditors of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carried on for any fraudulent purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is knowingly a party to the carrying on of the business in that manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 993(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`any business of a company is carried on` AND (`it is carried on with intent to defraud creditors of the company` OR `it is carried on with intent to defraud creditors of any other person` OR `it is carried on for any fraudulent purpose`))
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any business of a company is carried on with intent to defraud creditors of the company or creditors of any other person, or for any fraudulent purpose"
    ELSE IF `the person is knowingly a party to the carrying on of the business in that manner`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of "every person who is knowingly a party to the carrying on of the business in that manner"

-- s 993(2): the offence applies whether or not the company has been, or is in the course of being, wound up.
DECLARE `s 993(2) state of the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 993(2) wound up`
    `s 993(2) in the course of being wound up`
    `s 993(2) neither wound up nor in the course of being wound up`

-- src:13928 | (2) This applies whether or not the company has been, or is in the course of being, wound up.
@ref s 993(2) Offence of fraudulent trading (src:13928-13928)
GIVEN state IS A `s 993(2) state of the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 993(2) subsection (1) applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER state
    WHEN `s 993(2) wound up` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 993(2) in the course of being wound up` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 993(2) neither wound up nor in the course of being wound up` THEN JUST TRUE

-- s 993(3): the penalty: on indictment up to ten years or a fine (or both); on summary conviction twelve months (England and Wales) or six months (Scotland or Northern Ireland), or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
-- src:13929 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:13930 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years or a fine (or both);
-- src:13931 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:13932 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:13933 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 993(3) Offence of fraudulent trading (src:13929-13933)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 993(3) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 10, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives one penalty for England and Wales and another for Scotland or Northern Ireland, so a conviction not placed is not covered
